{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1196781-starting-a-game-have-some-questions","id":1196781,"title":"Starting a game, have some questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-18T07:03:39-07:00","id":1196781,"title":"Starting a game, have some questions","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:roboto\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Looks like my Exalted game is going on Hiatus and the next game is Changeling: the Lost. I will be using first edition (rules not 100% out yet for second edition, my group would not react well to beats) and have some questions...</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:roboto\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">-Any traps or major problems that are not too obvious in this edition?</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:roboto\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">-Any good actual plays I can listen to?</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:roboto\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">-A player wants to play a redcap from Changeling the Dreaming, with a delusion that it is that setting, I can't see this working and wonder what people think of this character.<br /> -Will have everyone work together to make up the NPCs and Power structure of the local Changeling population on the first session. Any good places that have some Apocolypse world style questions that could help?</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/363-muscadomestica","name":"MuscaDomestica","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T23:51:12-07:00","id":1213344,"title":"","content":"I know this response is a lil' late, but lemme see if I can help<br /> -Not sure, I haven't looked at it<br /> -Yes, &quot;At Sixes &amp; Sevens&quot; was a fantastic actual play podcast with the most hilarious session that ever happened during an RPG, recorded. Fandible also did a decent run.<br /> -I don't know much about C:tD, but your player could still play a traditional redcap. Maybe a variant of the Wizened or Darkling, and then put them in the Autumn court. Nasty creatures though...<br /> -Sorry, never played Apocalypse world. You could set it just in Mad Max Australia though...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24164-marengo","name":"Marengo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-01T14:06:11-07:00","id":1250531,"title":"","content":"Lost time is a recurring trope in fairy tales. Time of Judgment came out in 2004. Let your Redcap player create his player character but let him be temporally displaced from 2004. He remembers a reenactment of the first battle of Moytura' in which the Autumn People under the leadership of the Fir Bolg fought beside US military forces in Norfolk,VA against the combined might of the Tuatha de Danann and the Fomoire and lost; tearing the veil of banality and letting the dreaming come crashing into the physical world. He also remembers a flight of dragons descending on Washington DC. Now for him it is suddenly 14 years later: a has been 80's celebrity has somehow become president of the United States, the money no longer looks right, and cell phones have morphed from simple convenient flip devices into mind eating gadgets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1869-moonwolf8","name":"moonwolf8","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-01T15:13:06-07:00","id":1250546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>moonwolf8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1196781-starting-a-game-have-some-questions?p=1250531#post1250531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lost time is a recurring trope in fairy tales.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lost time has recurred in this thread.<br /> <br /> The World of Darkness crossover idea is cute, but Dreaming and Lost are different games with pretty different outlooks, and such a character probably isn't going to get on well with the typical Lost Courts. More importantly, it sounds like the kind of idea that a player would come up with if they just wish to play the old game and don't really want to learn the new one. That's a lack of necessary player buy-in if it's the case, and it's one that won't work out with the thematic differences between the two games. Lost has room for characters with the qualities of the typical redcap; that's classic Ogre territory. But the culture they live in, the place they come from, and the conflicts they fight aren't the same.<br /> <br /> Not that it matters much; this is probably not still a living issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-01T23:39:09-07:00","id":1250670,"title":"","content":"On the recap bit there are rules I'm 2e for creating your own Kith so that can be done easy enough that way. As to the delusion, with how different I hear the two are that might be quite difficult. A character with madness is one thing but a &quot;this game but my character sees it as that game&quot; just seems too meta to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}